    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00001",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 1,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Background.",
      "token_count": 4,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Background."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00002",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 2,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "Injection falls two spots from #3 to #5 in the ranking, maintaining its position relative to A04:2025-Cryptographic Failures and A06:2025-Insecure Design.\n\nInjection is one of the most tested categories with 100% of applications tested for some form of injection.\n\nIt had the greatest number of CVEs for any category, with 37 CWEs in this category.\n\nInjection includes Cross-site Scripting (high frequency/low impact) with more than 30k CVEs and SQL Injection (low frequency/high impact) with more than 14k CVEs.\n\nThe massive number of reported CVEs for CWE-79 Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting') brings down the average weighted impact of this category.",
      "token_count": 141,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Background."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00003",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 3,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Score table.",
      "token_count": 5,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
