        "Score table."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00005",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 5,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Description.",
      "token_count": 4,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Description."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00006",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 6,
      "chunk_type": "mixed",
      "text_content": "An injection vulnerability is an application flaw that allows untrusted user input to be sent to an interpreter (e.g.\n\na browser, database, the command line) and causes the interpreter to execute parts of that input as commands.\n\nAn application is vulnerable to attack when:\n\n* User-supplied data is not validated, filtered, or sanitized by the application.\n\n* Dynamic queries or non-parameterized calls without context-aware escaping are used directly in the interpreter.\n\n* Unsanitized data is used within object-relational mapping (ORM) search parameters to extract additional, sensitive records.\n\n* Potentially hostile data is directly used or concatenated.\n\nThe SQL or command contains the structure and malicious data in dynamic queries, commands, or stored procedures.\n\nSome of the more common injections are SQL, NoSQL, OS command, Object Relational Mapping (ORM), LDAP, and Expression Language (EL) or Object Graph Navigation Library (OGNL) injection.\n\nThe concept is identical among all interpreters.\n\nDetection is best achieved by a combination of source code review along with automated testing (including fuzzing) of all parameters, headers, URL, cookies, JSON, SOAP, and XML data inputs.\n\nThe addition of static (SAST), dynamic (DAST), and interactive (IAST) application security testing tools into the CI/CD pipeline can also be helpful to identify injection flaws before production deployment.\n\nA related class of injection vulnerabilities has become common in LLMs.\n\nThese are discussed separately in the [OWASP LLM Top 10](https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/), specifically [LLM01:2025 Prompt Injection](https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/).",
      "token_count": 339,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Description."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00007",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 7,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## How to prevent.",
      "token_count": 6,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "How to prevent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00008",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 8,
      "chunk_type": "mixed",
      "text_content": "The best means to prevent injection requires keeping data separate from commands and queries:\n\n* The preferred option is to use a safe API, which avoids using the interpreter entirely, provides a parameterized interface, or migrates to Object Relational Mapping Tools (ORMs).\n\n**Note:** Even when parameterized, stored procedures can still introduce SQL injection if PL/SQL or T-SQL concatenates queries and data or executes hostile data with EXECUTE IMMEDIATE or exec().\n\nWhen it is not possible to separate the data from commands, you can reduce threats using the following techniques.\n\n* Use positive server-side input validation.\n\nThis is not a complete defense as many applications require special characters, such as text areas or APIs for mobile applications.\n\n* For any residual dynamic queries, escape special characters using the specific escape syntax for that interpreter.\n\n**Note:** SQL structures such as table names, column names, and so on cannot be escaped, and thus user-supplied structure names are dangerous.\n\nThis is a common issue in report-writing software.\n\n**Warning** these techniques involve parsing and escaping complex strings, making them error-prone and not robust in the face of minor changes to the underlying system.",
      "token_count": 239,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "How to prevent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00009",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 9,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Example attack scenarios.",
      "token_count": 6,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00010",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 10,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "**Scenario #1:** An application uses untrusted data in the construction of the following vulnerable SQL call:",
      "token_count": 23,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00011",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 11,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\nString query = \"SELECT * FROM accounts WHERE custID='\" + request.getParameter(\"id\") + \"'\";\n```",
      "token_count": 33,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00012",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 12,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "An attacker modifies the 'id' parameter value in their browser to send: `' OR '1'='1`.\n\nFor example:",
      "token_count": 29,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00013",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 13,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\nhttp://example.com/app/accountView?id=' OR '1'='1\n```",
      "token_count": 28,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00014",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 14,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "This changes the meaning of the query to return all records from the accounts table.\n\nMore dangerous attacks could modify or delete data or even invoke stored procedures.\n\n**Scenario #2:** An application's blind trust in frameworks may result in queries that are still vulnerable.\n\nFor example, Hibernate Query Language (HQL):",
      "token_count": 65,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00015",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 15,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\nQuery HQLQuery = session.createQuery(\"FROM accounts WHERE custID='\" + request.getParameter(\"id\") + \"'\");\n```",
      "token_count": 36,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00016",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 16,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "An attacker supplies: `' OR custID IS NOT NULL OR custID='`.\n\nThis bypasses the filter and returns all accounts.\n\nWhile HQL has fewer dangerous functions than raw SQL, it still allows unauthorized data access when user input is concatenated into queries.\n\n**Scenario #3:** An application passes user input directly to an OS command:",
      "token_count": 69,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00017",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 17,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\nString cmd = \"nslookup \" + request.getParameter(\"domain\");\nRuntime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);\n```",
      "token_count": 33,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00018",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 18,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "An attacker supplies `example.com; cat /etc/passwd` to execute arbitrary commands on the server.",
      "token_count": 22,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A05:2025 Injection",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0_c00019",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a05_injection",
      "version_id": "ver_d617676bd8d0",
      "chunk_idx": 19,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## References.",
      "token_count": 4,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
